meta {
  name: Update Rate Limits
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/admin/teams/customer-support
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminApiKey}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "rate_limits": {
      "requests_per_minute": 60,
      "burst_capacity": 100
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Updates rate-limit parameters for a team — no gateway restart required.

  Requires the calling team to have `is_admin: true` in teams.yaml.
  The `product-search` team (apiKey env var) has admin access by default.

  The update is applied atomically to the in-memory resolver — requests
  already in flight keep their old limits; new requests pick up the new values
  immediately.

  The YAML file on disk is NOT updated — fold the change into source control
  separately to persist across restarts.

  Fields (all optional — omit to leave unchanged):
  - `rate_limits.requests_per_minute` — refill rate for the token bucket
  - `rate_limits.burst_capacity`      — maximum burst above the steady-state rate
  - `budget.daily_usd`                — daily USD cap
  - `allowed_models`                  — array of allowed model IDs
}
